# scry's opt-in path-traversal pack (CWE-22)
#
# This file is a small pack (command injection, format strings, the forbidden calls)
# plus a wider `path-traversal` rule, so `--rules lib/Scry/rules/path-traversal.scry`
# adds `argv` and the `realpath` sanitiser to the file-path sinks. It is opt-in; the
# default pack's own `path-traversal` rule has the call sources only (see
# scry/README.md, "Rules").
#
# Taint reaches a path API through `getenv`, `read`/`recv`/`fgets`/`getline`/
# `fread`, or C's `argv`. The `source argv result` line is a pack directive, not a
# call pattern: it seeds the second parameter of `main` as a source.
#
# `realpath` is modelled in `Scry.Models` as a sanitiser of its result and of the
# destination it writes (argument 1), never of its input. So
#
#   realpath(user, buf); open(buf);    -- clean: buf is the canonical path
#   realpath(user, buf); open(user);   -- still reported: the input is unchanged
#   p = realpath(user, 0); open(p);    -- clean: the result is canonical
#
# `sanitize_path`/`confine_path` are the policy-model sanitisers already in the
# model table. A program that normalises with its own function (as the Apache
# reduction for CVE-2021-41773 does) is not laundered: there is no model for it.

rule command-injection
  kind taint
  severity error
  message Attacker-controlled data reaches a command interpreter
  source getenv result
  source recv result
  source read arg 1
  sanitise escape_shell result
  sanitise shellescape result
  sanitise sanitize arg 0
  sink system arg 0
  sink popen arg 0
end

rule format-string
  kind taint
  severity warning
  message Attacker-controlled data is used as a format string
  source getenv result
  source recv result
  sanitise escape_shell result
  sink printf arg 0
  sink fprintf arg 1
end

rule gets-overflow
  kind forbidden
  severity error
  message gets cannot bound its write; use fgets with a size
  call gets
end

rule strcpy-overflow
  kind forbidden
  severity warning
  message strcpy does not bound the copy; use strlcpy or a checked length
  call strcpy
  call strcat
end

rule path-traversal
  kind taint
  severity error
  message Attacker-controlled data reaches a filesystem path
  source getenv result
  source recv result
  source read arg 1
  source fgets arg 0
  source getline arg 0
  source fread arg 0
  source argv result
  sanitise realpath result
  sanitise sanitize_path result
  sanitise confine_path result
  sink open arg 0
  sink openat arg 1
  sink creat arg 0
  sink fopen arg 0
  sink freopen arg 0
  sink stat arg 0
  sink lstat arg 0
  sink unlink arg 0
  sink remove arg 0
  sink rename arg 0
  sink rename arg 1
  sink chdir arg 0
  sink opendir arg 0
  sink access arg 0
  sink mkdir arg 0
  sink rmdir arg 0
end
